-- title:
--   Iterated Vélu j equals full-kernel quotient j
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, let $N$ be a nonzero natural number with $N \neq 0$ in $K$, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $K$ which is elliptic, and let $Q$ be a point of the affine model of $W$ whose additive order is exactly $N$. Form the one-shot Vélu curve `W.fullKernelQuotient Q N`: taking $S$ to be the finite set of pairs obtained as the images (via `coordsOrZero`) of the multiples $k \bullet Q$ for $1 \le k \le N-1$, and setting $t = \sum_{(x,y) \in S} g^x(x,y)$ and $w = \sum_{(x,y) \in S} \bigl(x\,g^x(x,y) - y\,g^y(x,y)\bigr)$ with $g^x(x,y) = 3x^2 + 2a_2 x + a_4 - a_1 y$ and $g^y(x,y) = -(2y + a_1 x + a_3)$, this is the Weierstrass curve with the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$ as $W$ and with $a_4 - 5t$, $a_6 - b_2 t - 7w$. Assume its discriminant $\Delta$ is nonzero. Then the quantity `W.cyclicQuotientJ (AddSubgroup.zmultiples Q) N`, namely $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the curve produced by the iteration `cqjIterate` applied to the subgroup $\langle Q \rangle$ generated by $Q$ and to $N$, equals the $j$-invariant of `W.fullKernelQuotient Q N`, the latter being formed using the invertibility of $\Delta$ furnished by the hypothesis.
--
--   Both sides are explicit Weierstrass models of the quotient of $W$ by the cyclic subgroup generated by $Q$: one built by iterating prime-degree Vélu steps, the other by Vélu's single sum over the nontrivial multiples of $Q$; the assertion is that the resulting elements of $K$ agree. It is used in the treatment of moduli points on modular curves, in [`ModularCurve.congrEquiv_moduliPlace_eq_moduliPlace_fullKernelQuotient_of_atkinLehner`](thm.html#ModularCurve.congrEquiv_moduliPlace_eq_moduliPlace_fullKernelQuotient_of_atkinLehner) and [`ModularCurve.moduliPlace_restrictAlong_qExpand_fullKernelQuotient`](thm.html#ModularCurve.moduliPlace_restrictAlong_qExpand_fullKernelQuotient).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_cyclicQuotientJ_zmultiples_eq_fullKernelQuotient_j.lean

